      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The perception of \"dodgy\" is often a mix of actual street activity and cultural discomfort for outsiders. Some people are genuinely intimidated by unfamiliar cultures or the visible differences in certain neighborhoods. It's less about a direct link between ethnicity and crime, and more about the social friction and the presence of different lifestyles that can feel unpredictable to a tourist. If you prefer a very predictable, homogenous experience, then the more affluent, less diverse areas will feel safer to your sensibilities.",
